  <section id="system" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">03 / DIGITAL INFRASTRUCTURE</span><div><h2>Web / <em>autonomy / decentralization.</em></h2><p>METHODOLOGY 01 / WEB. Experiment with autonomous platforms, self-hosting and distributed nodes as infrastructures of resistance. Examine how ownership, access, maintenance, deceleration and collective governance shape what can be researched and shared.</p><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 01 — DISTRIBUTED ARCHIVE / RELATIONAL INDEX</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 900 380" role="img" aria-label="Curved non-hierarchical archive connections"><g class="wires"><path d="M130 100C220 15 365 70 450 185S690 300 765 100M130 100C210 270 330 325 450 185S650 12 765 100M130 285C270 340 320 90 450 185S650 350 770 285M130 285C65 200 75 165 130 100M765 100C845 180 850 225 770 285M130 100C340 20 585 350 770 285"/></g><g class="accent-wires"><path d="M130 100Q330 165 450 185T765 100M130 285Q325 200 450 185T770 285"/></g><g class="nodes"><circle cx="130" cy="100" r="32"/><circle cx="130" cy="285" r="30"/><circle cx="450" cy="185" r="44"/><circle cx="765" cy="100" r="32"/><circle cx="770" cy="285" r="34"/></g><g text-anchor="middle"><text x="130" y="104">MEMORY</text><text x="130" y="289">SITES</text><text x="450" y="182">ARCHIVE</text><text x="450" y="195">/ INDEX</text><text x="765" y="104">ECOLOGY</text><text x="770" y="289">PEOPLE</text></g><g class="hyper-svg-stars"><text x="300" y="83">✳</text><text x="612" y="268">✦</text></g></svg></figure><p class="hyper-pink-note">★ ALLY OR CONTROL SYSTEM?</p><p>ALLIED TECHNOLOGIES = tools shaped with their users. DESIGN / MAINTAIN / REVISE / SHARE.</p><small>OBJECTIVE: decentralized platforms / independent publishing / shared and revisable governance.</small></div><div class="hyper-protocol"><div><span>HOST / OWNERSHIP</span><p>Where is the archive stored? Who can maintain it? Independence is a condition to negotiate, not a property guaranteed by software.</p></div><div><span>ACCESS / GOVERNANCE</span><p>Multiple contributors. Revisable metadata. Consent, attribution and withdrawal. Visibility must not become compulsory exposure.</p></div><div><span>PLATFORM DECENTRALIZATION</span><p>Test distributed publishing and interoperable archives. Decentralization is a technical and social question, not an automatic guarantee of autonomy.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="space" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">04 / PHYSICAL OUTPUT</span><div><h2>Archive / <em>physical device.</em></h2><p>METHODOLOGY 02 / PHYSICAL. Server sculptures, installative devices, parasitic architectures and guerrilla mapping are possible outputs, not predetermined deliverables. Physical and digital are porous, mutually transformative conditions of the same archive.</p><div class="hyper-server-study hyper-exit-focus"><span>ARTIST COLLABORATION / EXIT / PARTICIPATORY ARCHIVE DEVELOPMENT</span><h3>ARCHIVE OF THE UNTAMED / EXIT</h3><p>EXIT — Olivia Teglia and Lucia Fontanelli — is an artistic collaboration engaging with site-specific research, collective experimentation and public space. Their work intersects with Archive of the Untamed through shared inquiry into urban transformations, situated ecologies and collective memory.</p><p>Our collaboration explores the participatory development of Archive of the Untamed: ways of gathering situated contributions, building relationships with local communities and activating the archive through collective artistic practices and public encounters. Rather than imposing a fixed archival structure, the methods and forms of participation remain open to the people and contexts involved.</p><small>EXIT / OLIVIA TEGLIA + LUCIA FONTANELLI / PARTICIPATORY METHODOLOGIES / ONGOING COLLABORATION</small><a class="hyper-collab-link" href="https://www.instagram.com/_exitexitexit_/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="EXIT on Instagram">INSTAGRAM / @ _exitexitexit_ ↗</a></div><div class="hyper-server-study hyper-alma-focus"><span>ARTIST COLLABORATION / ALMA FUTURA / PROTOTYPE IN DEVELOPMENT</span><h3>SHELL AS HOST / ALMA FUTURA</h3><p>ALMA Futura approached me to develop a hyperarchive for their feminist collective research and self-education on bodies and technologies. Conceived as an autonomous infrastructure for knowledge and resistance, the proposed shell-shaped server sculpture could host the website, store research objects and become an educational device. Like a jellyfish head, its core could connect to modular hardware tentacles: screens, projectors, sensors and other interfaces. Funding is being sought.</p><small>ALMA FUTURA / ARTIST COLLABORATORS / CONCEPT IN DEVELOPMENT / FUNDING IN PROGRESS</small><a class="hyper-collab-link" href="https://www.instagram.com/_almafutura_/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="ALMA Futura on Instagram">INSTAGRAM / @_almafutura_ ↗</a></div><figure class="hyper-diagram hyper-io-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 02 — HYPERARCHIVE / INPUT → CORE → OUTPUT → FEEDBACK</figcaption><div class="hyper-io-flow"><div class="hyper-io-column"><span>01 / INPUTS</span><div>RESEARCH OBJECTS<small>material collections</small></div><div>MEDIA / RECORDS<small>images / audio / texts</small></div><div>COLLECTIVE CONTRIBUTIONS<small>knowledge / workshops</small></div></div><b>→</b><div class="hyper-io-column hyper-io-core"><span>02 / ARCHIVE CORE</span><div>SELF-HOSTED SERVER<small>database / web publishing</small></div><div>PHYSICAL STORAGE<small>research objects / care</small></div><div>MODULAR CONNECTIONS<small>hardware / protocols</small></div></div><b>→</b><div class="hyper-io-column"><span>03 / OUTPUTS</span><div>WEB INTERFACES<small>independent access</small></div><div>PHYSICAL DEVICES<small>screens / projections</small></div><div>EDUCATIONAL ACTIVATIONS<small>learning / encounters</small></div></div></div><div class="hyper-io-return">↖ FEEDBACK / NEW RECORDS / RECONFIGURATION / SHARED MAINTENANCE ↗</div><p>PHYSICAL ↔ DIGITAL. Objects become records; records activate devices; encounters generate new materials. Inputs and outputs are not fixed roles.</p></figure><div class="hyper-output-types"><div><span>01 / SERVER SCULPTURES</span><p>Self-hosted infrastructures as sculptural bodies.</p></div><div><span>02 / INSTALLATIVE DEVICES</span><p>Screens, projectors, sensors and modular interfaces.</p></div><div><span>03 / PARASITIC ARCHITECTURES</span><p>Temporary, flexible structures adapting to existing spaces.</p></div><div><span>04 / GUERRILLA MAPPING</span><p>Situated projections and interventions on public surfaces.</p></div></div><div class="hyper-columns"><div><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 03 — PROJECTION / URBAN SURFACE</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 420 300" role="img" aria-label="Conceptual urban facade transformed by a luminous projection"><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-opacity=".38"><path d="M32 258H388"/><path d="M112 84L315 64V258H112Z"/><path d="M112 84L94 101V258M315 64L337 83V258"/><path d="M138 115L172 112V146H138ZM197 109L231 106V140H197ZM258 103L292 100V134H258ZM138 168H172V203H138ZM197 165H231V200H197ZM258 162H292V197H258Z"/></g><g fill="none" stroke="#39ff14" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M112 206C165 124 239 124 315 171"/><path d="M112 140C175 209 240 213 315 109"/><path d="M112 234C174 187 243 181 315 228" stroke-opacity=".6"/></g><path d="M112 84L315 64V258H112Z" fill="#39ff14" fill-opacity=".035"/><g fill="none" stroke="#39ff14" stroke-width="1"><path d="M52 252L169 170M52 252L265 142" stroke-dasharray="3 7" opacity=".6"/><circle cx="52" cy="252" r="5"/></g></svg></figure><h3>03 / Guerrilla mapping</h3><p>INPUT: archive fragments / maps / audiovisual records. OUTPUT: temporary urban projection.</p></div><div><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 04 — PARASITIC / FLEXIBLE STRUCTURE</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 420 300" role="img" aria-label="Conceptual floating cube as a temporary suspended architecture"><g stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".22" fill="none"><path d="M70 50H354" stroke-dasharray="3 7"/><path d="M85 260H357" stroke-dasharray="3 7"/></g><g stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".5" stroke-width="1" fill="none"><path d="M114 50L135 108M296 50L296 108M135 108L209 152M296 108L209 152" stroke-dasharray="4 7"/></g><g fill="#39ff14" fill-opacity=".055" stroke="#39ff14" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M135 108L268 90L337 137L209 155Z"/><path d="M135 108L209 155V242L135 194Z"/><path d="M209 155L337 137V222L209 242Z"/></g><g fill="none" stroke="#39ff14" stroke-width="1.3"><path d="M135 108L209 155L337 137"/><path d="M137 174Q181 126 223 184T337 172"/><path d="M211 219Q276 161 337 205" stroke-opacity=".7"/></g><g stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity=".2" fill="none"><path d="M135 194L209 242L337 222"/><path d="M135 250L209 271L337 246" stroke-dasharray="3 7"/></g></svg></figure><h3>04 / Parasitic architectures</h3><p>FLEXIBLE / SITE-RESPONSIVE / COLLECTIVELY ASSEMBLED.</p></div></div><figure class="hyper-diagram"><figcaption>FIG. 05 — RECIPROCAL FEEDBACK / CURVED PATHS</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 900 260" role="img" aria-label="Curved reciprocal loop connecting archive, public interventions and new contributions"><g class="accent-wires"><path d="M180 130C280 12 370 12 450 130S640 248 730 130"/><path d="M730 130C650 8 555 8 450 130S280 252 180 130" stroke-dasharray="5 8"/><circle cx="180" cy="130" r="48"/><circle cx="450" cy="130" r="48"/><circle cx="730" cy="130" r="48"/></g><g text-anchor="middle"><text x="180" y="125">CRITICAL</text><text x="180" y="139">MAPPING</text><text x="450" y="125">DIGITAL</text><text x="450" y="139">AUTONOMY</text><text x="730" y="125">NEW SPACES</text><text x="730" y="139">OF KNOWLEDGE</text><text x="450" y="27">NEW TRACES / RETURN / REASSEMBLY</text></g></svg></figure></div><div class="hyper-protocol"><div><span>DEBOUNDING</span><p>Public/private is not a stable binary. Examine who sets thresholds, grants access, monitors use and authorises presence.</p></div><div><span>TRANSLATION</span><p>Documents become projections, temporary structures and encounters. Spatial translation changes the reading of the archive; it does not simply display it.</p></div><div><span>FLEXIBILITY</span><p>Site-responsive interventions that adapt to different spaces, uses and local relationships. Their forms and duration remain open to negotiation and change.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="human" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">05 / RELATIONAL GENERATION</span><div><h2>People / <em>relational generation.</em></h2><p>METHODOLOGY 03 / RELATIONAL. Collective self-education, workshops, shared archival practices and networks of contributors sustain spaces of resistance. Knowledge is produced, contested and cared for together, at tempos negotiated by participants.</p><p>RESEARCH → SHARE → REINTERPRET → ACTIVATE → CARE. Movements and collectives shape the archive through their practices, needs and decisions; the archive can in turn support their capacity to organise and transmit knowledge.</p><figure class="hyper-diagram hyper-relational hyper-relational-system"><figcaption>FIG. 04 — RELATIONAL INFRASTRUCTURE / A RECIPROCAL SYSTEM</figcaption><svg viewBox="0 0 900 510" role="img" aria-label="A relational system: situated people and knowledge contribute to a shared archive, the archive activates devices and spaces, encounters generate new contributions, and collective governance maintains all three."><defs><marker id="rel-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L6 3L0 6" fill="none" stroke="#39ff14" stroke-width="1.1"/></marker><marker id="rel-arrow-muted" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L6 3L0 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1"/></marker></defs><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" opacity=".5"><rect x="30" y="142" width="235" height="145" rx="2"/><rect x="332" y="142" width="235" height="145" rx="2"/><rect x="635" y="142" width="235" height="145" rx="2"/><rect x="267" y="382" width="365" height="82" rx="2"/></g><g fill="none" stroke="#39ff14" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#rel-arrow)"><path d="M265 206H326"/><path d="M567 206H629"/><path d="M754 287C755 352 661 351 632 351H140C103 351 100 316 100 291"/></g><g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".65" stroke-dasharray="4 5" marker-end="url(#rel-arrow-muted)"><path d="M450 382V290"/><path d="M334 422C210 422 148 382 148 291"/><path d="M567 422C690 422 752 382 752 291"/></g><g fill="currentColor" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif"><text x="30" y="44" font-size="13" fill="#39ff14">RESEARCH / SOCIAL / MATERIAL</text><text x="30" y="67" font-size="23">Contributions do not end at publication.</text><text x="48" y="169" font-size="12" fill="#39ff14">01 / CONTRIBUTE</text><text x="48" y="203" font-size="18">PEOPLE + KNOWLEDGE</text><text x="48" y="231" font-size="12">objects / experiences / skills</text><text x="48" y="250" font-size="12">collective documentation</text><text x="350" y="169" font-size="12" fill="#39ff14">02 / ORGANISE</text><text x="350" y="203" font-size="18">SHARED ARCHIVE</text><text x="350" y="231" font-size="12">metadata / access / relations</text><text x="350" y="250" font-size="12">self-hosted infrastructure</text><text x="653" y="169" font-size="12" fill="#39ff14">03 / ACTIVATE</text><text x="653" y="203" font-size="18">DEVICES + SPACE</text><text x="653" y="231" font-size="12">workshops / projections</text><text x="653" y="250" font-size="12">public encounters</text><text x="390" y="403" font-size="12" fill="#39ff14">04 / SUSTAIN</text><text x="295" y="431" font-size="17">COLLECTIVE GOVERNANCE + CARE</text><text x="315" y="451" font-size="12">decisions / maintenance / responsibilities</text><text x="275" y="194" font-size="10" fill="#39ff14">SHARE</text><text x="580" y="194" font-size="10" fill="#39ff14">DEPLOY</text><text x="328" y="337" font-size="11" fill="#39ff14">NEW RELATIONS / RECORDS / QUESTIONS</text></g></svg><p>Contributions are organised into a shared archive; its materials activate educational and spatial situations; those encounters generate new contributions. Governance and maintenance support the whole cycle — they are not another output.</p></figure><p class="hyper-pink-note">★ A platform connects records. People construct infrastructures.</p></div><div class="hyper-protocol"><div><span>RELATION</span><p>Nodes are not interchangeable users. They are people, situated practices, uneven capacities, dependencies and shared commitments.</p></div><div><span>ASSEMBLY</span><p>The interface can facilitate contact. Collective decisions, trust, conflict and maintenance happen through human negotiation.</p></div><div><span>RHIZOME / TEST</span><p>Multiple entrances and lateral links. No mandatory centre. How does a network remain open without erasing responsibility?</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="loop" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">06 / THE LOOP</span><div><h2>Web ↔ matter ↔ <em>people.</em></h2><p>METHOD: collective contributions ↔ autonomous web archive ↔ physical manifestations ↔ relational generation. Each iteration can revise the others.</p><div class="hyper-loop" aria-label="Critical mapping loop"><div class="hyper-loop-step"><span>01 ★ WEB INFRASTRUCTURE</span><p>Independent platforms / self-hosting / distributed nodes.</p></div><div class="hyper-loop-arrow">↓</div><div class="hyper-loop-step"><span>02 ★ PHYSICAL OUTPUT</span><p>Server sculpture / projections / spatial installations.</p></div><div class="hyper-loop-arrow">↓</div><div class="hyper-loop-step"><span>03 ★ RELATIONAL GENERATION</span><p>Workshops / shared practices / collective encounters.</p></div><div class="hyper-loop-return">↖ NEW CONTRIBUTIONS / REVISE THE METHODOLOGY ★</div></div></div><div class="hyper-protocol"><div><span>FEEDBACK</span><p>New encounters generate new accounts. Participants may challenge the archive's categories, priorities or public visibility.</p></div><div><span>NO FINAL VERSION</span><p>Each iteration tests how web infrastructure, physical devices and human relationships reshape one another.</p></div></div></section>
  <section id="process" class="hyper-section"><span class="hyper-index">07 / TWO-MONTH RESIDENCY</span><div><h2>Research / <em>prototype / deploy.</em></h2><div class="hyper-steps"><p><strong>W01–02</strong>Case studies / collaborators / archival and hosting audit.</p><p><strong>W03–04</strong>Web methods / decentralized hosting tests / server-sculpture sketches.</p><p><strong>W05–06</strong>Prototype physical outputs / hosting enclosure / projections / integration.</p><p><strong>W07–08</strong>Relational activation / test / document / revise methods.</p></div><div class="hyper-columns"><div><h3>Artist contribution</h3><p>Web / code / audiovisual / mapping / laptop.</p></div><div><h3>Host / local collaboration</h3><p>Fabrication / projector / AV / local access / permits.</p></div></div><small>TARGET: working archive iteration + site-responsive installation. FORMAT: context-dependent.</small></div></section>
